cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CAML in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "CAML: Benchmarking open-source AutoML frameworks in isolated environments"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tabatabaei
    given-names: Ali
version: 1.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-24
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/A1i-Tabatabaei/CAML"
url: "https://github.com/A1i-Tabatabaei/CAML"
abstract: >-
  CAML installs the major open-source AutoML frameworks (AutoGluon, H2O
  AutoML, FLAML, LightAutoML, MLJAR-supervised, TPOT, GAMA, FEDOT, TabPFN,
  SapientML) at pinned versions, each in its own isolated uv environment, and
  benchmarks them on OpenML suites or a user's own tabular data with
  resumable sweeps, per-dataset leaderboards and paired significance tests.
  It is a from-scratch rewrite inspired by the OpenML AutoML Benchmark.
keywords:
  - automl
  - benchmark
  - machine learning
  - tabular data
  - reproducibility
